Leave your materials where you keep them. Better Crafting saves you from collecting them cabinet by cabinet before using the workbench.

[size=5]Craft from any storage[/size]
[list]
[*][b]One click fills the workbench.[/b] Select a recipe in Crafting Notes, and the game's own fill takes the missing materials from home storage. Craft Again, dye choices, and batch crafts work too.[/*]
[*][b]See what you can craft.[/b] Recipe material counts, availability borders, and the batch "Max" include home storage.[/*]
[*][b]Your tabs first.[/b] Materials come from the open tab, then your backpack, the Workbench Drawer, and Tool Cabinets, then other home storage. In each place, the game picks the items by its own rule.[/*]
[*][b]You choose when to craft.[/b] Review the filled grid, then click Craft.[/*]
[/list]
Only storage in unlocked areas of your home is included. If you don't have enough materials for the recipe, nothing moves. When you click Clear, items from home storage go to the open tab, not back to their storage.

The mod adds your home storage to the game's own list of places for the fill, so the game fills and moves the materials with its own code and follows its storage access rules. It changes no game file and writes nothing of its own to the save, so you can remove it at any time.

[size=5]Compatibility[/size]
Use either Better Crafting or [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/4]BaseButler[/url]. If both are installed, Better Crafting disables Craft from any storage to avoid conflicts. The differences, compared with BaseButler 2.0.2:
[code]+--------------+---------------------------+-----------------+
|              | BaseButler 2.0.2          | Better Crafting |
+--------------+---------------------------+-----------------+
| Windows      | workbench, cooking, trade | workbench only  |
| Game files   | modifies 3 game files     | no change       |
| Storage      | also outside your home    | your home only  |
| Storage tabs | a tab for each storage    | no extra tab    |
| Craft        | starts it by itself       | you click Craft |
+--------------+---------------------------+-----------------+[/code]
To switch from BaseButler to Better Crafting, delete [font=Courier New]BepInEx\plugins\BaseButler.dll[/font]. BaseButler's changes to game files remain after you remove its DLL. Restore those files through Steam: in the Library, right-click Survival Log > Properties > Installed Files > Verify integrity of game files. Steam restores only the game's own files: BepInEx and your other mods stay.

[size=5]Requirements[/size]
[list]
[*]Survival Log 1.1.18153 or later. On an older game version, this version turns itself off. For game version 1.0.17573, use Better Crafting 1.0.0 under Files.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/12]BepInEx for Survival Log[/url]. Install it first.[/*]
[/list]
[size=5]Installation[/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/12]BepInEx[/url] [i](if no other mods were installed before, start the game once so BepInEx finishes setup, then quit)[/i].[/*]
[*]Extract this mod's zip into the game folder (the folder with the game .exe). The DLL lands in BepInEx\plugins. Full path example:
[list]
[*]Steam:
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Survival Log\BepInEx\plugins\BetterCrafting.dll[/code]
[/*]
[/list]
[/*]
[/list]
[size=5]Uninstall[/size]
Delete [font=Courier New]BetterCrafting.dll[/font] from the [font=Courier New]BepInEx\plugins[/font] folder.

[size=5]Configuration[/size]
To change mod settings, edit [font=Courier New]BepInEx\config\com.ivmakk.survivallog.bettercrafting.cfg[/font] while the game is closed (see [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-sl/sl-better-crafting/blob/main/CONFIG.md]CONFIG.md[/url] for every setting). Changes apply at the next game start.

